    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192-a2">

                <pb facs="0265" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg999"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Butler to Mr. Mariscal.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Most respectfully I beg to submit the
                    statement prepared by Mr. William Farmer Forsee and his attorney, Sr. Lie.
                    Francisco Alfaro, in the matter of the extradition of the Rowe brothers.</p>
                <p>I beg that you will give this communication careful perusal and grant it due
                    weight in the consideration of the case. Trusting that the opinion of my
                    Government, as quoted to your excellency on the 23d instant, and the legal
                    deductions set forth in the inclosed statement may lead your excellency to grant
                    the extradition of Chester and Richard Rowe, I beg most sincerely to renew to
                    your excellency the assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. C. Butler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
